 the LAN. Do not put Kubernetes on the QSFP nets."},"3428":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-27","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#1-node","content":"No inter-node NCCL. Local multi-GPU (if advertised) uses SHM/P2P. The `highspeed` inventory group is ignored."},"3429":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-28","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"Each physical QSFP cage appears as two Linux netdevs (two PCIe x4 twins). One cable brings one cage up — do not assume both cages are populated."},"3430":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-29","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"Existing 1-node / 2-node Jobs and `group_vars` document:"},"3431":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-30","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"Also typically `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=0`. Confirm names with `ibdev2netdev` on **your** nodes before baking env."},"3432":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-31","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"kimi / kimi-test omit `hostNetwork` (isolation). Heavy Ray / GLM-5.2 Jobs set `hostNetwork: true` (and GLM `hostIPC: true`) so IFNAME is visible."},"3433":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-32","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"200 Gb/s per physical port — not NVLink, not an IB switch. Triangle:"},"3434":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-33","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Port0 = cage next to the RJ-45 jack; Port1 = far cage. Wrong polarity looks half-alive."},"3435":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-34","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Mode B (GLM-5.3-Flash TP=3) and Mode C (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP=3) Jobs set:"},"3436":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-35","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Plus `hostNetwork: true` and `hostIPC: true`. If 10GbE is not `enP7s7`, set `LAB_MGMT_IFNAME`. Mode C also cuts `NCCL_BUFFSIZE=1MiB`."},"3437":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-36","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"`highspeed_interfaces: enp1s0f0np0,enp1s0f1np1` is the pair reference. Ring Jobs in `k8s/workloads/glm-5.3-flash/` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash/` already have the ring block."},"3438":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-37","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Full cabling, aliases, and util caps: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"3439":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-38","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"},"3440":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-39","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**4 nodes:** one full CRS804 port per node (`sfpplus1`…`sfpplus4`). The Spark CX-7 link is 200 Gb/s."},"3441":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-40","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**5 nodes:** three full ports + one port split with a breakout cable into\n`sfpplus4a` / `sfpplus4b` (two 200G lanes). Both lanes must be declared in the\n`switch.port_map` — the topology validator rejects a lone lane."},"3442":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-41","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Each link is its own /24 (192.168.110–114, MTU 9000) from the generated per-node\nnetplan — one node per subnet, so there is no shared-suffix IP scheme to get wrong."},"3443":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-42","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` stays the management NIC; the payload rides the single RoCE HCA\n(`NCCL_IB_HCA` from live `ibdev2netdev` names per node)."},"3444":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-43","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Heavy Jobs use `hostNetwork: true`. Do not assume the 2-node pair\n`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` list is complete — it is not, on a switch."},"3445":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-44","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."},"3446":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-45","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"After `start-test` on a pair:"},"3447":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-46","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"Expect the high-speed IFNAME in the NCCL init lines, not the management NIC as payload."},"3448":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-47","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"If logs show fallback to `eth0` / 10GbE for all-reduce, stop the Job (`bazelisk run //:manage -- stop`) and fix netplan / Job env before retrying a heavy TP Job."},"3449":{"id":"/learn","page_id":"/learn","type":"page","content":"Learn the lab","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Learn the lab"],"tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn"},"3450":{"id":"/learn-0","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn","content":"Short operator track — K3s on DGX Spark, Resource Guard, NCCL fabrics, and why heavy jobs never auto-start."},"3451":{"id":"/learn-1","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Learn the lab"},"3452":{"id":"/learn-2","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"K3s on Spark"},"3453":{"id":"/learn-3","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Resource Guard (not Compose occupancy)"},"3454":{"id":"/learn-4","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#nccl","content":"NCCL"},"3455":{"id":"/learn-5","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#why-no-auto-start","content":"Why no auto-start"},"3456":{"id":"/learn-6","page_id":"/learn","type":"heading","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"url":"/learn#next","content":"Next"},"3457":{"id":"/learn-7","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"**What's on this page**"},"3458":{"id":"/learn-8","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Why this lab is K3s Jobs, not Compose demos"},"3459":{"id":"/learn-9","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Resource Guard headroom in one paragraph"},"3460":{"id":"/learn-10","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"NCCL pair vs ring"},"3461":{"id":"/learn-11","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Why reboot does not bring inference back"},"3462":{"id":"/learn-12","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"**What this enables**"},"3463":{"id":"/learn-13","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Reading later operate pages without tripping on jargon"},"3464":{"id":"/learn-14","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Not treating ez-comfy-stack occupancy rules as this cluster's capacity gate"},"3465":{"id":"/learn-15","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"This is **not** a ComfyUI beginner course. Still images and video on one Spark with Docker Compose: ez-comfy-stack."},"3466":{"id":"/learn-16","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"Each GB10 node is one GPU, 20 Arm cores, 128 GB unified memory. Kubelet reservations and Resource Guard keep SSH and K3s alive while Jobs request most of the rest."},"3467":{"id":"/learn-17","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"spark0 runs the K3s **server** and a **worker**"},"3468":{"id":"/learn-18","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"spark1+ are agents"},"3469":{"id":"/learn-19","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"GPU Operator installs drivers, device plugin, DCGM"},"3470":{"id":"/learn-20","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"Bootstrap is Ansible. Day-2 mutations go through `manage.sh` (`bazelisk run //:manage -- …`) so confirmations and capacity checks stay in one place."},"3471":{"id":"/learn-21","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"ez-comfy-stack talks about **occupancy** of a Compose project. This lab uses **Resource Guard**:"},"3472":{"id":"/learn-22","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Policy: `config/resource-policy.yaml` (edit YAML first, JSON twin second)"},"3473":{"id":"/learn-23","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Runtime: `scripts/lib/resources.sh` on `start-*`"},"3474":{"id":"/learn-24","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Kubernetes: PriorityClass, ResourceQuota, LimitRange"},"3475":{"id":"/learn-25","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Floor: **max(24Gi, 15% of allocatable) per node** — not a second 64Gi tax after kubelet"},"3476":{"id":"/learn-26","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","content":"Mode A vLLM `--gpu-memory-utilization` ≤ **0.82**. Mode B exclusive ≤ **0.85**. Mode C SGLang `--mem-fraction-static` ≤ **0.95**. Never ship vLLM 0.88/0.90."},"3477":{"id":"/learn-27","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#resource-guard-not-compose-occupancy","